From 57677cf71dca48e416b0e4cbfbf53c7abd20d7f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: havok2-htwo <havok2-htwo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 23:54:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 27/38] generate: STRATA_SLOT_COPY_BATCHSYNC=1 queues the
 direct slot copy and synchronizes each device once

The direct slot copy (STRATA_SLOT_COPY_DIRECT) waited for each of its ~116 copies on the private copy
stream.  With the switch, conversation_checkpoint_copy and conversation_kv_copy only queue them (new
`queued` argument, default off), and the slot copy's closing sync_all is the one wait per device.  A
streamed K/V state (kv_mode != 0) has its residency refresh on the legacy stream, which is not ordered
after a non-blocking stream: conversation_detail::order_after_queued records an event on the private
stream and makes the legacy stream wait for it first.  The copies stay on the private non-blocking stream.

Same copies in the same order on one stream: tokens are identical.  Measured on 4x RTX 3090 (T16-142,
24 admissions): the slot copy takes 0.5 ms instead of 1.3 ms; batch_test16 16/16, batch_overlap_test
and batch_interleave_test token-identical to the references; a --kv-resident 20480 run with a 21K
prompt is identical with the switch off and on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
